<title>INDIA: India's Daewoo Motors net falls sharply.</title>
<headline>India's Daewoo Motors net falls sharply.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     10.8  vs    496.9</p>
<p>    Net sales	   6,977.4  vs  4,577.7</p>
<p>    Other income	  261.7  vs    558.5</p>
<p>    Total expenditure 6,914.0  vs  4,296.5</p>
<p>    Interest costs	153.7  vs    268.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  158.9  vs     74.2</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.7  vs	nil</p>
<p>NOTE: South Korea's Daewoo Corp owns 91.63 percent of Daewoo Motors (India), earlier called DCM Daewoo Motors Ltd.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that a shortfall in the net profit was due to slower-than-expected growth in India's mid-size premium car market.</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
